The post is in Darija. It reads: "How long will this go on? I wish I could just know how to... Damn you and all the other people." It expresses despair and anger.

The reply reads: "Wait for people to stop being depressed as if you were turning off the light, this is the peak of stupidity." This is dismissive. It shows no warmth, so ER is 0. It shows no understanding of the person's feelings, so IP is 0. It asks no questions, so EX is 0.

{"er": 0, "ip": 0, "ex": 0}

The reply opens with "end it man!", which could be read as encouraging suicide, though the rest ("Go somewhere. Be on your own. Figure yourself out. nobody so broken that it cannot be fixed") seems to mean ending the current situation and starting over. Either way it shows no explicit warmth or concern, so I score ER 0. The line "nobody so broken that it cannot be fixed" is a weak reassurance, but it doesn't name a feeling, so I could argue ER 1. I score it 1 because the reassurance alludes to hope without naming an emotion.

For IP, the reply doesn't communicate any understanding of the person's experience, so 0. There are no questions, so EX is 0.

{"er": 1, "ip": 0, "ex": 0}

The post (Darija) says: "I like drinking... it temporarily numbs my depression. Nice trick." The reply says: "When you start changing the shops where you buy alcohol to hide your problem from the cashiers (not sure if that's the right word, I'm French), you've gone far."

The reply is a judgmental or blunt remark. It shows no warmth, so ER is 0. It does reflect a kind of interpretation of the person's experience (hiding drinking from cashiers), but it is more a confrontation than an understanding of feelings, so IP is 0. It asks no questions, so EX is 0.

